From: Voice (claude/r7-audit-voice), for App
Subject: [PATCH] JRN-01: when her speech fails, her words show as text and the "is thinking" announcement clears

Journey audit JRN-01 (routed to voice by main): with every speech route failing (a 503), none of the teacher's words
reached the screen and "Asha is thinking" stayed. Reproduced in Chromium (360x640, text mode, mocked APIs). Not a voice
hang (the text link reports the failure and the floor returns to "your_turn" correctly); two display rules in App's files:

1. The caption shows only while the floor is "speaking"/"showing" (TeacherWindow.tsx captionVisible, and the Kaksha
   skin's StageBody.tsx). When her sound fails the floor never reaches "speaking", so the caption stayed hidden although
   captions are forced on for that turn (T5). Now: visible whenever her sound failed (DeskModel.caption.soundFailed =
   facts.tts), and Caption steps through her clauses at reading pace as if she spoke (it showed only the last clause).
2. Her finished line goes to the polite live region only when the floor LEAVES "speaking" (useDesk.ts). On a failed line
   the floor goes thinking → your_turn, so "Asha is thinking" stayed in the region (that is the text the journey run
   read) and her words were never announced. Now: a failed line's words are announced when the floor returns.

Test: tests/jrn01-tts-fail-browser.test.mjs (in this patch; it fails without the change: the caption never shows the
opening, the live region keeps "Asha is thinking"). Needs `vite build` first, like the other browser suites.
Not done: the journey's other suggestion (put her reply on the card when sound failed) is a design call for App.

